From e232d7846e055a966f942ec24eb3c7e1d928f309 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel <champion327@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 19:47:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add dedicated three-column PDF/print layout

- New src/resume-pdf.njk builds /print/, a standalone executive-length
  layout (header + sidebar/2-col experience/earlier-career strip)
  instead of reusing the on-screen page's stripped print CSS.
  Bilingual (reads ?lang= or the stored site preference), auto-opens
  the print dialog once fonts are ready, with a manual print/back/lang
  fallback bar that is hidden in the printed output.
- Download PDF button now opens /print/ in a new tab instead of
  printing the live page.
- resume.js: added the 'location' field index.njk already referenced
  but never had (was rendering blank), plus PDF-specific UI strings
  (statsTitle, pdfFooterNote, pdfPrintButton, pdfBackLink) in both
  languages.
---
 src/_data/resume.js |  10 +
 src/index.njk       |  22 +-
 src/resume-pdf.njk  | 479 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 493 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/resume-pdf.njk

